#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:2
msgid ""
"Return or set the :attr:`~pyvista.DataSet.points` dtype used by filters and "
"sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:4
msgid ""
"Many VTK algorithms generate single-precision points even when the input has"
" double-precision points, and a few do the reverse, so the ``points`` dtype "
"can change underneath you partway through a pipeline. This setting makes the"
" dtype a property of the session rather than of whichever algorithm happens "
"to run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:9
msgid ""
"Where it is not ``None`` it is enforced everywhere PyVista wraps the output "
"of a VTK algorithm, which covers every filter, every geometry and parametric"
" source, and the generated points of :class:`~pyvista.ImageData` and "
":class:`~pyvista.RectilinearGrid`. Constructing a dataset keeps the array "
"you pass, so ``pv.PolyData(points)`` has the dtype of ``points``; the "
"geometry factories are sources, so ``pv.Triangle(points)`` follows the "
"setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:16
msgid "``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:17
msgid ""
"The default. PyVista does not intervene and each algorithm produces whatever"
" dtype it produces, which is the behavior of every release before 0.49."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:21
msgid "``'preserve'``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:22
msgid ""
"A filter's output points have the same dtype as its input points, so a "
"filter never changes the dtype. This covers the meshes that store their "
"points; :class:`~pyvista.ImageData` and :class:`~pyvista.RectilinearGrid` "
"generate theirs from the origin and spacing, or from the coordinate arrays, "
"so they constrain nothing. Sources have no input either, and keep the dtype "
"VTK generates. A filter that builds one of those as an intermediate takes "
"the dtype from it rather than from the input, so "
":meth:`~pyvista.DataSetFilters.voxelize` and "
":meth:`~pyvista.PolyDataFilters.reconstruct_surface` still produce single "
"precision from a double-precision mesh. Ask for ``'float64'`` where the "
"output dtype has to be certain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:34
msgid "``'float32'``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:35
msgid ""
"Every source and filter generates single-precision points, including the "
"ones that would otherwise generate double precision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:38
msgid "``'float64'``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:39
msgid "Every source and filter generates double-precision points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:41
msgid ""
"Copying or recasting a dataset is not a source and keeps the points it was "
"given, so ``mesh.copy()`` and ``mesh.cast_to_pointset()`` never change "
"dtype."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:46
msgid ""
"A dtype can always be delivered; the precision behind it cannot. Some "
"algorithms cannot run in double at all -- :vtk:`vtkShrinkFilter` has no "
"precision setting -- so they compute in single and their output is cast back"
" up. The points are then ``float64`` holding values that are only single "
"precision, and calling "
":meth:`~pyvista.core.pointset._PointSetBase.points_to_double` on them "
"recovers nothing: the digits went when the filter ran. A ``float64`` points "
"array is not on its own evidence of double-precision values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:55
msgid ""
"Every such cast warns with :class:`~pyvista.PrecisionWarning`, naming the "
"algorithm, so the fabrication is never silent. Casting the other way does "
"not warn: discarding digits below the input's own representation error loses"
" nothing that was there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:60
msgid ""
"The setter accepts ``'preserve'``, ``None``, and anything "
":class:`numpy.dtype` resolves to ``numpy.float32`` or ``numpy.float64`` (for"
" example ``np.float64``, ``'double'``, or ``float``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:75
#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.show_vtk_api:36
#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.validate_on_wrap:22
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:77
msgid ""
"An explicit ``'float32'`` or ``'float64'`` is requested from the algorithm "
"first, via ``SetOutputPointsPrecision``, so the computation itself is done "
"in that precision wherever VTK supports it, and only the algorithms that "
"ignore the request need their output cast afterwards. ``'preserve'`` asks "
"for nothing: VTK's own default already matches the input for all but a "
"handful, and requesting it anyway would widen more than the points for some "
"filters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype:84
msgid ""
"That request reaches whatever else the algorithm generates at the same "
"precision, so an explicit dtype is not confined to the points. Transforming "
"a mesh with :meth:`~pyvista.DataObjectFilters.transform` and "
"``transform_all_input_vectors=True`` under ``'float64'`` gives the "
"transformed vector arrays ``float64`` as well, doubling their memory. Arrays"
" the filter does not transform keep the dtype they had."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/user-guide/configuration.rst:6
msgid ""
"By default a filter produces whatever VTK produces, and "
":vtk:`vtkShrinkFilter` produces single precision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/user-guide/configuration.rst:17
msgid ""
"Ask for the dtype to survive the filter instead. It does, and because this "
"filter cannot compute in double, the widened points are reported as holding "
"single-precision values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/user-guide/configuration.rst:32
msgid ""
"Treat that as an error instead wherever the fabricated precision is not "
"acceptable. This is a standard warnings filter, so it can be scoped to a "
"block, a module, or a whole session, and set from ``-W`` or pytest as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/user-guide/configuration.rst:44
msgid "Sources follow the setting too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.show_vtk_api:2
msgid "Return or set whether VTK-inherited attributes appear in :func:`dir`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.show_vtk_api:4
msgid ""
"When ``False`` (the default), attributes inherited from VTK base classes are"
" hidden from :func:`dir` and tab-completion on PyVista objects that wrap VTK"
" types (data objects, :class:`~pyvista.Renderer`, :class:`~pyvista.Actor`, "
":class:`~pyvista.Property`, etc.). This keeps the public surface curated for"
" data-science IDEs such as Positron's Variables pane and VS Code's Jupyter "
"extension, and for IPython / Jupyter tab-completion. VTK methods remain "
"fully callable regardless of this setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.show_vtk_api:13
msgid ""
"When ``True``, the full VTK API is enumerated alongside the PyVista API, "
"which is useful for VTK developers who want to discover the raw VTK method "
"surface via introspection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.show_vtk_api:19
msgid ""
"This option requires runtime inspection and does not work with all developer"
" tools, for example, it has no effect when using PyCharm. This is because it"
" relies on calling the object's ``__dir__`` method for generating auto-"
"completion suggestions. Tools like PyCharm that only use static analysis for"
" auto-completion are therefore unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.show_vtk_api:38
msgid ""
"The ``snake_case`` VTK aliases (``number_of_points``, ``deep_copy``, and so "
"on) are controlled separately by :func:`pyvista.vtk_snake_case`. When "
"``snake_case`` is not ``'allow'`` (the default), those names are hidden from"
" :func:`dir` regardless of this setting, because accessing them would "
"already raise ``PyVistaAttributeError``. Enabling ``snake_case`` surfaces "
"the ``snake_case`` names in :func:`dir`; ``show_vtk_api`` only controls the "
"CamelCase VTK API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.validate_on_wrap:2
msgid "Return or set whether :func:`pyvista.wrap` validates data arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.validate_on_wrap:4
msgid ""
"When ``True`` (the default), :func:`pyvista.wrap` performs a cheap array-"
"length sanity check on every VTK object it wraps and emits a "
":class:`~pyvista.InvalidMeshWarning` if any point or cell data array has a "
"tuple count that does not match the dataset's point or cell count. Set to "
"``False`` to skip this check globally when the cost matters in tight loops "
"and the caller trusts their inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/config.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.config.Config.validate_on_wrap:24
msgid ""
"Per-call control is also available via the ``validate`` keyword on "
":func:`pyvista.wrap`, :func:`pyvista.read`, and "
":meth:`pyvista.BaseReader.read`. The per-call keyword takes precedence; this"
" global setting is consulted only when the per-call keyword is left at its "
"default ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/user-guide/configuration.rst:84
msgid ""
"The warning emitted when "
":attr:`~pyvista.core.config.Config.validate_on_wrap` finds an invalid data "
"array:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/errors.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.errors.InvalidMeshWarning:2
msgid "Warning for invalid mesh properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/user-guide/configuration.rst:90
msgid ""
"The warning emitted when :attr:`~pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype` "
"asks an algorithm for double-precision points it cannot generate, so the "
"output is cast up and the dtype ends up wider than the values behind it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/errors.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.errors.PrecisionWarning:2
msgid "Warning that points could not be generated at the requested precision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/errors.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.errors.PrecisionWarning:4
msgid ""
"Raised when :attr:`pyvista.core.config.Config.points_dtype` asks for a wider"
" dtype than the VTK algorithm that ran can generate. The output points are "
"cast up so that the dtype is the one asked for, but the values they hold "
"have the precision the algorithm produced, and casting cannot bring back "
"digits it already discarded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/errors.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.errors.PrecisionWarning:10
msgid ""
"The message names whatever generated the points: the VTK class for a filter,"
" the PyVista class for a source, since a source is its own algorithm, and "
"the library for a hull computed outside VTK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/errors.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.errors.PrecisionWarning:14
msgid ""
"Being a warning rather than an error is what keeps the choice with the "
"caller. Escalate it where the fabricated precision is not acceptable::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/errors.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.errors.PrecisionWarning:19
msgid "or silence it where it is::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.15/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/errors.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.errors.PrecisionWarning:23
msgid ""
"Either can be scoped to a block with :class:`warnings.catch_warnings`, or "
"set for a run from ``-W`` or a test runner's own configuration."
msgstr ""

